What:   line-mode session restore (session_restore_mode = { lines = N }, shpool's default
        engine) redraws the last N lines of output, up to and including the cursor's row, and
        leaves the cursor on that row. Before, it drew the N rows above the cursor's row and put
        the cursor at its old absolute row, below what it drew: on reattach the prompt was
        missing and the cursor was in empty space, whenever more than N rows of output were on
        the screen.
Where:  src/grid.rs (last_n_rows, write_cursor_position_formatted_at), src/screen.rs
        (last_n_rows_contents_formatted), tests/window_contents.rs (four round-trip tests:
        what a terminal shows after the restore).
Shape:  fixes behaviour; the public write_cursor_position_formatted is unchanged.
Needs:  nothing before it. Applies to shpool_vt100 v0.1.3 (vt100/), not to shpool.
Status: to be offered upstream (shell-pool/shpool_vt100).

